5. Build reproducibility (what is known, and what is NOT shipped)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This section exists so a reader can judge how much of this binary is traceable.
It does NOT ship source code, and no upstream project maintains this build.

5.1  What is pinned by this repository
     - The shipped binary itself, by hash (section 4). Only one build is
       published: sha256 B07D9FCF...8B31891E, built 2026-10-20 07:36.
     - The launch flags, the calibration tooling and every measured number
       (AGENTS.md / README.md), so the *behaviour* of this build is reproducible
       even though its source is not.

5.2  What is NOT published
     - The engine source tree. It is a local, unpublished fusion build
       (`infer-build/fusion-arch-20261019`), not derived from a single public
       commit that could be checked out.
     - Upstream commit SHAs. This build is descended from the NInfer 0.11.0
       line (1.2) but carries additional merged work (section 2) that has no
       public counterpart, so naming a commit would be misleading.

5.3  Consequence: this is NOT a reproducible build
     Building an identical binary is not possible from public information.
     Verify integrity by hash (section 4, and the Release `.sha256` /
     `.manifest.txt` attachments), not by rebuilding.

5.4  This build is not an official release of any upstream project
     Nothing here is endorsed by, or supported by, the projects listed in
     sections 1.1-1.5. Bug reports about this binary should not be filed
     upstream. Known defects are listed in README.md under "已知问题".

